    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0014" n="8" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg8"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.24/51: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-07-01T12:00:00-05:00">July 1,
                            1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>71. Department’s telegraphic instruction June 27, 7 p.m. discussed with Minister
                    of Foreign Affairs afternoon of June 29 when he stated he desired to present the
                    matter to the President before expressing an opinion. Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs has just orally declared that the Panaman Government enthusiastically
                    endorses the plan to extend the facilities of American Government owned yards
                    and arsenals to the other American Republics. He added that such a policy is not
                    only necessary but also indispensable in the present state of world affairs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
